From 82831bb4370ac52c56585a5625004013a97282fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Michaud <jmichaud@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:19:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/23] [mya] Run testLibJSCTools with OS_ACTIVITY_MODE=disable
 on Cocoa Need the bug URL (OOPS!).

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

Test harness environment only.

run-javascriptcore-tests runs testLibJSCTools with OS_ACTIVITY_MODE=disable
on Apple Cocoa ports.

Why it is needed: Xcode's LLDB.framework records an os_signpost and an
os_log message for every SB API call. The heap walk makes SB API calls for
every type and field it reads, so with logging on, the walk takes about
twice as long, and the HeapWalk and DebugInfo suites with it.

What we lose if it is not taken: nothing functional; testLibJSCTools is
slower on macOS. Only meaningful after the LLDB.framework patch.

* Tools/Scripts/run-javascriptcore-tests:

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Tools/Scripts/run-javascriptcore-tests | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Tools/Scripts/run-javascriptcore-tests b/Tools/Scripts/run-javascriptcore-tests
index 34ec9b5511a2..f88b694b55de 100755
--- a/Tools/Scripts/run-javascriptcore-tests
+++ b/Tools/Scripts/run-javascriptcore-tests
@@ -839,7 +839,8 @@ if ($runTestAPI) {
     runTest("testapi", "allApiTestsPassedWithSystemMalloc", "Malloc=1");
 }
 if ($runTestWasmDebugger) { runTest("testwasmdebugger", "allWasmDebuggerTestsPassed") }
-if ($runTestLibJSCTools) { runTest("testLibJSCTools", "allLibJSCToolsTestsPassed") }
+# Xcode's LLDB.framework records an os_signpost and an os_log message per SB API call, which doubles the heap walk.
+if ($runTestLibJSCTools) { runTest("testLibJSCTools", "allLibJSCToolsTestsPassed", isAppleCocoaWebKit() ? "OS_ACTIVITY_MODE=disable" : "") }
 
 # Find JavaScriptCore directory
 chdirWebKit();
